# Line endings.
#
# The repo is uniformly LF (verified: 0 of 869 TypeScript sources carried CRLF
# when this was added), so `eol=lf` is a no-op on existing content and causes no
# renormalisation churn. It is here to keep it that way: a checkout on Windows
# with core.autocrlf=true would otherwise hand every contributor CRLF working
# copies, and the next tool that rewrites a file bakes that into a commit.
#
# .githooks/pre-commit reads these attributes rather than hardcoding its own
# exemption list, so anything declared binary or eol=crlf below is left alone.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the real exception: some interpreters need CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touch, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
